37.Scenario: K-Means Clustering for Customer Segmentation
You are working for an e-commerce company and want to segment your customers into distinct groups
based on their purchasing behavior. You have collected a dataset of customer data with various
shopping-related features.
Write a Python program that allows the user to input the shopping-related features of a new customer.
The program should use K-Means clustering from scikit-learn to assign the new customer to one of the
existing segments based on the input features.

# Experiment 37
# K-Means Clustering for Customer Segmentation

import pandas as pd
from sklearn.cluster import KMeans
from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler

# --------------------------------------------------
# STEP 1: Get number of customers
# --------------------------------------------------

n = int(input("Enter number of customers: "))

data = []

print("\nEnter customer shopping details:")

for i in range(n):

    print("\nCustomer", i + 1)

    income = float(input("Enter Annual Income: "))
    spending = float(input("Enter Spending Amount: "))
    frequency = float(input("Enter Purchase Frequency: "))
    loyalty = float(input("Enter Loyalty Points: "))

    data.append([
        income,
        spending,
        frequency,
        loyalty
    ])

# --------------------------------------------------
# STEP 2: Create DataFrame
# --------------------------------------------------

df = pd.DataFrame(data, columns=[
    "Income",
    "Spending",
    "Purchase_Frequency",
    "Loyalty_Points"
])

print("\n========== CUSTOMER DATA ==========")
print(df)

# --------------------------------------------------
# STEP 3: Standardize features
# --------------------------------------------------

scaler = StandardScaler()

X_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(df)

# --------------------------------------------------
# STEP 4: Enter number of clusters
# --------------------------------------------------

k = int(input("\nEnter number of customer segments (K): "))

# --------------------------------------------------
# STEP 5: Create K-Means model
# --------------------------------------------------

kmeans = KMeans(
    n_clusters=k,
    random_state=42,
    n_init=10
)

kmeans.fit(X_scaled)

# --------------------------------------------------
# STEP 6: Assign clusters
# --------------------------------------------------

df["Cluster"] = kmeans.labels_

print("\n========== CUSTOMER SEGMENTS ==========")
print(df)

# --------------------------------------------------
# STEP 7: Display cluster centers
# --------------------------------------------------

centers = scaler.inverse_transform(kmeans.cluster_centers_)

center_df = pd.DataFrame(
    centers,
    columns=[
        "Income",
        "Spending",
        "Purchase_Frequency",
        "Loyalty_Points"
    ]
)

print("\n========== CLUSTER CENTERS ==========")
print(center_df)

# --------------------------------------------------
# STEP 8: Enter new customer
# --------------------------------------------------

print("\n========== NEW CUSTOMER ==========")

income = float(input("Enter Annual Income: "))
spending = float(input("Enter Spending Amount: "))
frequency = float(input("Enter Purchase Frequency: "))
loyalty = float(input("Enter Loyalty Points: "))

new_customer = [[
    income,
    spending,
    frequency,
    loyalty
]]

# --------------------------------------------------
# STEP 9: Standardize new customer
# --------------------------------------------------

new_customer_scaled = scaler.transform(new_customer)

# --------------------------------------------------
# STEP 10: Predict customer segment
# --------------------------------------------------

cluster = kmeans.predict(new_customer_scaled)

print("\n========== PREDICTION ==========")

print("New customer belongs to Segment:",
      cluster[0] + 1)
